      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Plasma concentrations of soluble tumor necrosis factor alpha (TNF-alpha) receptor type I (sTNF-RI) were assessed in two complex regional pain syndrome (CRPS) patient groups (n = 30 and n = 16) and healthy controls (n = 25). Patients with CRPS and mechanical hyperalgesia had higher levels of sTNF-RI (1,661.8 +/- 146.8 pg/mL) compared with those with CRPS with identical clinical appearance but without hyperalgesia (1,155.9 +/- 56.3 pg/mL) and controls (1,239.5 +/- 42.9 pg/mL). This study suggests involvement of TNF-alpha in mechanical hyperalgesia of CRPS."},
